  "id": "Compound::DB01053 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Benzylpenicillin, a member of the Penicillin class of antibiotics, is linked to Slc15a1 through a series of indirect but consistent pathways. The evidence suggests that Benzylpenicillin, as part of the broader Penicillin family, binds to Slc15a1 through its inclusion in subgroups like Oxacillin and Dicloxacillin, which themselves interact with Slc15a1. This indicates a potential mechanism where the structural or functional properties of Penicillins, particularly their ability to bind to specific transporters, contribute to their interaction with Slc15a1. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Slc15a1, despite varying intermediate steps, supports a general role of Penicillins in modulating Slc15a1 activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on Penicillins' pharmacological properties to influence Slc15a1, suggesting a broader functional relationship that is both mechanistically plausible and biologically relevant.",
